---
// FAQ Accordion + From Algarve to the World — two-panel section
---

<section class="two-panel-section faq-growth-section">
  <!-- LEFT: FAQ Accordion -->
  <div class="panel panel-left">
    <div class="panel-inner">
      <span class="section-label">Frequently asked questions</span>
      <h2>Your Questions,<br/>Answered</h2>

      <div class="faq-accordion">
        <details class="faq-item" open>
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">What is FollowBirds?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>FollowBirds is a birdwatching app for Portugal. It helps you discover birds, join guided tours, track sightings, and keep detailed records of every birdwatching experience.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">Do I need to join a tour?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>No. You can use FollowBirds independently to explore the bird library, find birding hotspots, and track your personal sightings. Tours are optional.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">How do guided tours work?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Guides create tours from reusable templates and invite participants via email, link, or QR code. During the tour, everyone shares live sightings. At the end, FollowBirds automatically generates a detailed report.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">How do participants receive tours?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Participants receive an invitation by email or a shareable link/QR code. Once accepted, the tour appears directly in their FollowBirds account.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">Can guides create reusable templates?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. Guides can build tour templates with pre-set routes, species checklists, and notes, then reuse them to create new dated tours effortlessly.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">Can I export reports?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. Reports can be exported as PDF, shared via a web link, or accessed directly within the FollowBirds app.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">Can reports include weather information?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. Tour reports automatically include weather conditions recorded during the tour.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">Can bird names be shown in different languages?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. FollowBirds supports multilingual bird names, showing English, Portuguese, and scientific names.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">Who can become a guide?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Any birding professional or enthusiastic guide who leads tours in Portugal can apply. Email <a href="mailto:guides@followbirds.com">guides@followbirds.com</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q">How much will the guide platform cost?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Early guide program access is currently free. Pricing will be announced before the guide platform formally launches.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- DIVIDER -->
  <div class="panel-divider"></div>

  <!-- RIGHT: From Algarve to the World -->
  <div class="panel panel-right">
    <div class="panel-inner">
      <span class="section-label">Starting in Algarve, Growing through the community</span>
      <h2>From Algarve<br/>to the World</h2>
      <p class="panel-subtitle">
        FollowBirds begins with Portugal's rich birdlife and birding destinations. As guides create tours and experiences, new routes, locations, and birdwatching knowledge become available to the community.
      </p>

      <div class="growth-visual">
        <div class="growth-image-frame">
          <div class="growth-art">
            <!-- Illustrated coast scene -->
            <div class="coast-sky"></div>
            <div class="coast-water"></div>
            <div class="coast-ground"></div>
            <div class="coast-bird bird-1">🦅</div>
            <div class="coast-bird bird-2">🐦</div>
            <div class="coast-bird bird-3">🦢</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="growth-stats">
        <div class="growth-stat">
          <div class="growth-stat-num">450+</div>
          <div class="growth-stat-lbl">Bird Species</div>
        </div>
        <div class="growth-stat">
          <div class="growth-stat-num">30+</div>
          <div class="growth-stat-lbl">Birding Hotspots</div>
        </div>
        <div class="growth-stat">
          <div class="growth-stat-num">🌍</div>
          <div class="growth-stat-lbl">Growing Global</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .two-panel-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 4px 1fr;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .panel {
    padding: 5.5rem 0;
  }

  .panel-left .panel-inner {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin-left: auto;
    padding: 0 3rem 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .panel-right .panel-inner {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin-right: auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem 0 3rem;
  }

  .panel-divider {
    background: #EDE8DF;
    align-self: stretch;
  }

  .panel-subtitle {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #5E6B60;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  /* ── FAQ Accordion ── */
  .faq-accordion {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid #EDE8DF;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #EDE8DF;
  }

  .faq-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary:hover {
    background: #FAF7EF;
  }

  .faq-item[open] > summary {
    background: #FAF7EF;
  }

  .faq-q {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #142016;
    flex: 1;
    padding-right: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-toggle {
    color: #2F7D32;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-toggle {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 1.25rem 1rem;
    animation: fadeIn 0.2s ease;
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: #5E6B60;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .faq-answer a {
    color: #2F7D32;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  @keyframes fadeIn {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-4px); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  /* ── Growth visual ── */
  .growth-visual {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .growth-image-frame {
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    aspect-ratio: 4/3;
    position: relative;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
  }

  .growth-art {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
  }

  .coast-sky {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    height: 55%;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #87CEEB 0%, #B8E4F9 100%);
  }

  .coast-water {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 20%; left: 0; right: 0;
    height: 35%;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #5BA4CF 0%, #3D7EB5 100%);
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .coast-ground {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    height: 25%;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #7CB87B 0%, #5A9C59 100%);
  }

  .coast-bird {
    position: absolute;
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    animation: floatBird 4s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .bird-1 { top: 15%; left: 20%; animation-delay: 0s; }
  .bird-2 { top: 22%; left: 55%; font-size: 1.2rem; animation-delay: -1.5s; }
  .bird-3 { top: 10%; left: 72%; font-size: 1.5rem; animation-delay: -3s; }

  @keyframes floatBird {
    0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }
    50%       { transform: translateY(-6px); }
  }

  .growth-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .growth-stat {
    background: #FAF7EF;
    border: 1px solid #EDE8DF;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .growth-stat-num {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #2F7D32;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .growth-stat-lbl {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: #5E6B60;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .two-panel-section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .panel-divider {
      display: none;
    }

    .panel {
      padding: 4rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #EDE8DF;
    }

    .panel:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
    }

    .panel-left .panel-inner,
    .panel-right .panel-inner {
      max-width: 680px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
